.TH mygrep 3 "September 2026" "Version 1.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search for a string in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBmygrep\fR function scans the file \fBfp\fR line by line for occurrences of \fBsearch_str\fR. Matching lines are dynamically allocated and stored in an array of strings pointed to by \fBmatches\fR. It returns the total number of matches found, or -1 if any argument is NULL or memory allocation fails.
